<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Senate approves central bank chief.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Senate approves central bank chief.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's Senate approved the appointment of Central Bank President Pedro Pou Wednesday.</p>
<p>Pou has served as acting president since the former president, Roque Fernandez, took over the post of economy minister on July 26, replacing Domingo Cavallo.</p>
<p>Before his appointment, Pou was vice president at the Central Bank.</p>
<p>-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 54 1 3180668</p>
